== 2026-11-21 04:37:53 #1025 D 18 (B), the coordinator's order of 2026-11-21 04:3x: is the hybrid's sign trustworthy at D 18? Written before the run.
Why: the D 18 hybrid root run (lane_d18.sh) read -, +, - on its +-2% grid (1.75293, 1.78870, 1.82448), two sign changes, both robust to its
1e-15 noise test, so it fails rule (b) and no lambda is read at D 18 (d18_criteria.log). The bisection of its lower interval (near 1.7749777)
finishes and its root is recorded as information only. The leap to D 18.5 stays off until this is settled.
State and system: winb's leap state sol_l1kc63W1025_D18.000000.npy (blob 45e72c6a), k_c 63, Ks 30, u0 0.04, kappa 0.7, rk 1 (ell_ddm._setup's
settings, the record's; the root run's system check passed: |F| 2.6296e-10 against 2.6303e-10, 2552 steps).
Runs, in order, one process, 4 threads, nice 10 (lane_d18b.sh, after lane_d18.sh and lane_d185.sh exit):
  1. planted control: ell_ddm.py selftest must PASS, and ell_ddm.py selftest --mutate=slices must FAIL; otherwise stop.
  2. the hybrid at lam 1.8 (d18_hybsign.py, blob e089207a: p4_hybrid's sd(), with its 1e-15 noise test; the hybrid at 1.788704083622953, the
